  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In February 2020, the Central Organization of Trade Unions of Kenya (COTU-K) developed advocacy documents on employment, international labour standards, social protection, social dialogue and climate change, presented for negotiation at DWCP tripartite forums. 

COTU-K&apos;s advocacy paper on climate change influenced and shaped the government&#x2019;s decision of setting the goal of achieving a carbon neutral economy by 2050, through the implementation of a Sovereign Green Bond and an Emissions Trading System.

COTU-K advocated for transformation of the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) into a full-fledged pension scheme, extending social protection coverage to workers in the informal economy, and integrated employment retention benefit in the list of contingencies covered by the current social security scheme, as well as providing universal tax-financed pension coverage. 

Following advocacy of COTU-K, the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection signed Bilateral Labour Agreements (BLAs) with Saudi Arabia and Qatar and appointed Labour Attach&#xE9;s in its embassies in these two countries. Furthermore, Kenya is developing a national policy on labour migration that aims, among other things, to address gaps in legislation for private employment agencies and control unscrupulous organizations that are involved in human trafficking and child labour. In the period between January and February 2020, ILO provided technical assistance that enabled COTU-K to develop advocacy position papers on employment, international labour standards, social protection, climate change and social dialogue.

ILO further assisted COTU-K in identifying key messages that were used to develop promotional materials including flyers, posters, leaflets, etc. for its environmental protection campaigns.</narrative>
   </description>
